.\" robodr-support-bundle(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-ops/src/bin/robodr-support-bundle.rs and the module docs
.\" of crates/robodr-ops/src/{bundle,redact}.rs. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-SUPPORT\-BUNDLE 8 "2026-10-31" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-support\-bundle \- collect a redacted diagnostics bundle for RoboDR support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-support\-bundle
.RB [ \-\-out\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR TIME ]
.RB [ \-\-journal\-lines
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-journal ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-tar ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects what RoboDR support needs to diagnose a unit into
.IB DIR /robodr\-support\- HOST \- UTC .tar.gz
(mode 0600) and prints its path; the archive's SHA-256 goes to stderr.
Run it as root for the complete picture (journal, nftables, every status
file). Review the bundle before you send it: it is yours.
.SS Collected
.IP \(bu 2
OS release, kernel, uptime, memory, free space, network interfaces, time
synchronisation;
.IP \(bu 2
the RoboDR package state and
.B dpkg \-\-verify
/
.B rpm \-V
(modified files), the SHA-256 of every installed
.B robodr\-*
program;
.IP \(bu 2
the state of every
.B robodr*
unit
.RB ( "systemctl show" :
restarts, results, memory and CPU) and its unit files with drop-ins
.RB ( "systemctl cat" ,
redacted);
.IP \(bu 2
the journal of the
.B robodr*
units and the kernel for
.B \-\-since
(default
.BR \-48h ,
at most
.B \-\-journal\-lines
lines, default 20000), redacted;
.IP \(bu 2
.BR "nft list ruleset" ;
.IP \(bu 2
the daemons' status files
.RI ( status.json ", " uplink\-status.json ,
\&...), redacted;
.IP \(bu 2
count and total size of the files in the black box, the spool queues, the
diode outbox and the kept releases (never names or content);
.IP \(bu 2
the configuration files directly in
.I /etc/robodr
.RI ( *.json ", " *.toml ", " *.env ", " *.conf ),
redacted;
.IP \(bu 2
this host's
.B robodr\-setup preflight
and the current
.B robodr\-metrics
output.
.SS Never collected
Keys and credentials
.RI ( /etc/robodr/keys ", " /etc/robodr/kafka ", " /etc/robodr\-depot/keys ,
.IR /etc/robodr\-anchor\-receiver ", " /run/credentials ),
evidence
.RI ( /var/lib/robodr/blackbox ),
findings (the spool queues), control-plane state and evidence exports,
diode batches, commissioning workspaces, archives, fleet, delivery, depot
and executor state, release packages. Files are read only from explicit
paths, a symlink is never followed, and every path is checked against this
list (it is also in the manifest as
.BR never_collected ).
.SS Redaction
A value whose name reads like a secret
.RB ( secret ", " password ", " passphrase ", " token ", " private ,
.BR psk ", " api_key ", " hmac ", " bearer ", " authorization ", " cookie ,
.BR sasl ,
or a name that is or ends in
.B key
such as
.BR hmac_key ,
except
.BR public_key " and " pub_key )
is replaced by
.BR <redacted> ,
unless the name says it is a reference
.RB ( *_file ", " *_path ", " *_dir ", " *_socket ", " *_id ", " *_ids ):
a key file's path helps support, the key does not. JSON is redacted
structurally, other text line by line
.RB ( NAME=value ", " "NAME = value" ", " \(dqname\(dq: " value ,
.BR Environment=NAME=value );
PEM private-key blocks are dropped whole.
Whatever the name, the user information of every URL
.RB ( scheme://user:password@host )
is replaced by
.BR <redacted> ,
in JSON strings and in text.
.SS Fail closed
Before the bundle is packed, every file is scanned for key material (PEM
and OpenSSH private keys, minisign secret keys, RoboDR secret key files).
Any hit deletes the whole bundle and exits 1, naming the file: report that
to RoboDR support without the bundle.
.SS Layout
.TP
.I manifest.json
format
.BR robodr\-support\-bundle/1 :
every file with its size, SHA-256, source command or path, and whether it
was redacted; every item that could not be collected and why; the
never-collected list.
.TP
.I SHA256SUMS
.B sha256sum \-c
format, over every file including the manifest.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-dir " DIR"
where the bundle is written (default
.IR /var/tmp ).
.TP
.BI \-\-since " TIME"
journal window, a
.BR journalctl (1)
time such as
.B \-48h
or
.BR "\(dq2026\-10\-30 12:00\(dq" .
.TP
.BI \-\-journal\-lines " N"
most journal lines of the RoboDR units (default 20000).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-journal
leave the journal out.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tar
leave the bundle as a directory (0700).
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
read files under
.I DIR
instead of
.I /
(tests, a mounted image).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the bundle was written.
.TP
.B 1
failed, or key material was found (nothing is left behind).
.TP
.B 2
usage error.
.PP
Commands run with a fixed search path, an empty environment, a 30 s
timeout and bounded output; a missing command is recorded in the manifest,
not an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-setup (8),
.BR robodr\-metrics (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/SECURITY.md
